Assume BaseJsonValidator is abstract; test likely uses a concrete subclass. But we just need test case definitions.

Potential exception scenarios:

1. pathType is null -> atPath throws NullPointerException when trying to call append on null. To trigger, need to instantiate a subclass with pathType null. Provide test description.

2. currentPath is null and token is null -> pathType.append may throw NullPointerException or IllegalArgumentException. Provide test expecting NPE.

3. token contains illegal characters for PathType.SLASH? Actually slash can accept any token? Might not throw. For JSON_POINTER, token containing unescaped '~' or '/' is allowed but will be escaped; not exception.

Maybe PathType.append may throw IllegalArgumentException if token contains illegal characters like null character. We can assume.

Thus we propose test groups:

- Null pathType scenario
- Null token scenario
- Both parameters null scenario
- Invalid token scenario (e.g., token contains control character causing IllegalArgumentException)

